      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "dog_breed_stereotype",
      "label": "Dog Breed Stereotype",
      "description": "The question 'so which breed is your dad?' escalates the insult by implying the father (a man) is a specific, undesirable type of dog, reinforcing the dehumanizing and derogatory stereotype. This relies on real-world knowledge of dog breeds and their associated negative connotations (e.g., 'pit bull' as aggressive, 'chihuahua' as small and fragile, etc.), which are culturally understood as metaphors for undesirable human traits.",
